WEBVTT

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:23.400
In the heart of Africa, a young family is heading for an epic adventure.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.280
They are moving with their three children to a remote Kenyan wilderness.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:33.840
Mum Saba is here to run a safari camp...

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.000
Welcome!

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.520
..While dad Frank is helping to protect elephants...

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.800
Collar's almost on.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.240
Now the scary bit.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.920
..But raising a family and running a business in the bush is going to be a massive challenge.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.920
There are monkeys in the kitchen...

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.200
Oh, you monkeys, I'm going to kill you!

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:55.720
..Floods threatening the camp...

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.960
It's looking like it's going to be a mega storm.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.720
..And wildlife in need of help.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.160
Now my heart really is in my mouth.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.200
It's going to be a huge gamble.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:09.000
Will the business survive Saba's first season in charge?

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.240
Oh, my God.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.400
This time, a power crisis strikes camp.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.640
I'm just having such problems with this.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.040
It's driving me absolutely crazy.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:24.280
With the start of high season, it's a disaster.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:27.920
Saba's pulled away to a medical emergency...

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.960
It's bad and it needs urgent action.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.680
..And Frank is called out to help an injured lioness.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:40.240
Could be a snake bite, she could have been hit by a car, but we just don't know.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:54.600
Samburu National Reserve in northern Kenya.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:02:00.600
It's six in the morning and Saba is already out searching for lions to show her guests.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:09.880
They come here for top-notch safaris, so she must make sure she knows where to find every animal.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:20.600
Lions in Samburu are mostly nocturnal, so the key thing is to get up hellishly early in the morning and get out to wherever you think they are at first light.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:27.840
Top of her wish list - young cubs.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:34.320
To have new cubs, you know, the first cubs in quite a long time, is just so exciting.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.800
I can't quite believe it.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:44.840
She's looking for pawprints along the road so she can track them down as soon as the sun rises.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.360
This is real lion habitat here.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.320
They love this saltbrush.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.480
They could be anywhere here.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:57.400
It's extremely difficult to find them if you don't find their tracks in the morning.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:03.600
Staying one step ahead of the animals is essential because this is the busiest week of the season.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:14.360
Elephant Watch Camp has room for 12 guests in six luxury tents.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:20.680
With camp running at full capacity, they can't afford anything to go wrong.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:26.000
Wildlife guide Bernard is off to pick up the first of the new arrivals.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:33.120
I'm so excited to meet new people every time because it gives me an opportunity to show them what we have here.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:37.600
This season, this is the first time we're having a full camp.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.840
It's going to be a very intense period.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.600
So far this season, guest bookings have been down.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:52.240
For the business to succeed, the team must make sure everything runs like clockwork.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:57.080
Saba is still searching for lions.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.200
Look!

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:57.840
There!

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.680
There, there, there, there!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.800
There's the lioness.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.680
So exciting!

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:13.960
Those two cubs are tiny still.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.600
They're probably about six, seven weeks old.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:26.080
(So wonderful. )

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:39.160
The reserve is home to 40 lions living in three separate prides.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:46.040
The Koitogor Pride is the largest and they are all known by name.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:50.240
The oldest female is called Nabo.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:57.160
She has two five-year-old daughters.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:04.280
Now she's a grandmother and the Koitogor Pride has a third generation.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:11.080
It's one of Nabo's daughters who has given birth to these young cubs.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:22.320
These little guys are the grandchildren of the first lioness that I ever got to know, here in Samburu.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:30.560
She's now a really old female, who's called Nabo, which means "one" in Samburu, because she used to have one block black spot on her nose.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:38.440
Yeah, and she's still very much an important presence in this pride, and sticks around the central area of Samburu.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:41.080
In fact, she will definitely be having some contact with these cubs.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:45.520
It's exactly what Saba had hoped for.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:49.200
The reserve's newest arrivals are just in time for high season.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:56.120
This is absolutely wonderful because, when our guests arrive, this is one of the best things that we can come out and show them.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.480
Oh!

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.560
They are so sweet.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:07.960
With the cubs found, she returns to greet her guests.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:18.440
Back at camp, the team is ready and waiting.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:25.120
Hello, I'm Saba.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.240
I'm Shamila.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.840
Nice to meet you.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:36.120
Just when it seems everything is under control, there's bad news.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.000
Oh, God.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:41.000
Nothing's freezing.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:45.760
We've got serious problems with our solar system right now.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:50.480
And, look, you see, none of the ice is freezing.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.320
This has been here all night and it still hasn't frozen.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:53.520
I just don't know where the problem is.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:07:00.080
I don't know if we've got a short somewhere, or if it's the batteries, or if it's the solar panels or what.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:09.800
The camp is designed to run on solar energy, but the ageing system is no longer powerful enough to run the freezers.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:15.440
Most of the time, the guests haven't got a clue of what is going on and that's exactly how it should be.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:21.280
But I just need to make sure that they have the experience of a lifetime when they come here and they don't know about any of my issues behind-the-scenes.

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:37.520
Saba needs to do everything she can to get the power back on before her clients notice.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:51.320
Across the reserve, at the Save The Elephants headquarters, Saba's husband Frank has received worrying news.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.360
There's a wounded lion out in the park.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:08:02.880
It's about 20 minutes downriver, so I'm just going to go out and have a look at it, and see if there's anything we can do.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:12.800
The reserve's lion research team are away and Frank is closest to the scene.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.280
There's a few different possibilities of what could have happened to this lioness.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:19.640
It could be a snake bite, she could have been hit by a car, but we just don't know.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.920
So, we're just going to have a look before we start making any guesses.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:34.720
Back at camp, the guests have no idea there's a power problem.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:38.280
Saba has managed to get hold of energy expert Bart Fugers.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:41.400
So, come, let me show you the solar panels.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.880
Yep.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:48.840
Luckily, Bart was working at a nearby lodge, so he's dropped everything to come and help.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.680
So, these are our panels up here.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.280
Yep.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:58.040
We never get through the night so, in the evenings, we're having to put the generator on from six o'clock, and even with that, by five o'clock in the morning, all the power's gone.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:00.520
It's not just the freezers Saba's worried about.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:08.560
There's not enough power to charge the guests' cameras and phones.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.160
The system needs a scale-up.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:15.800
The solar panels, which need replacement, it's going to be a big investment.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:18.360
It's not going to be a quick fix.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:19.080
At the start of high season, this is the last thing Saba needs.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.960
The whole camp relies on solar power.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:26.840
Everything from, you know, all the lights and the fridges and the freezers - absolutely everything.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:32.600
Because we're so remote here, we can't get onto the mains and, you know, we're an eco-camp.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:39.200
We don't believe in having some huge great generator with a whole lot of disgusting fumes coming out of it.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:47.120
But the problem is our system is quite old now and it's in urgent need of an upgrade, and I'm really, really struggling to get enough power.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.960
But her problems are about to get even worse.

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:52.720
A member of camp is ill.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.600
I've got a sick person here.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.160
Let me come back.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:57.720
I just have to go and deal with this.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.200
Let me find out what's going on.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.560
Latoya.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:04.000
Malaria?

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:10.480
I think I might have to take him to the clinic, right now.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:22.840
Yup.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:28.880
I just have to take this guy to the clinic.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:29.520
Are you OK getting on with everything here on your own?

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.920
OK, I'm coming right now.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:45.240
If somebody gets sick out here, they'll sit at home and they'll deal with it until it gets really bad, so by the time to me and they need to go to a clinic, it's bad and it needs urgent action.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:51.280
So, I mean, the thing is, if you don't treat malaria, it can kill you.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:11:00.720
Latoya must be tested while he still has a fever, but it's 20 minutes to the closest clinic.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.640
Frank is dealing with his own emergency.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:07.080
He's found the injured lioness.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:11.600
She's lying under a tree.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:13.400
And...

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:17.280
I've stayed a little distance away, but it's not looking very good.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:21.360
It doesn't look like she's breathing.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.800
I can't see any movement at all.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:38.920
Frank has alerted the park rangers and he's updating the reserve's lion expert Shivani Bhalla, who has studied these lions for 12 years.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.960
Hi, Shiv?

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.600
'Yeah?'

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.560
We've just arrived and she seems to have stopped breathing.

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.280
It doesn't look good at all.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:55.960
They are too late to help.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.440
Oh, what a tragedy.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:01.680
You know, there are so few lions left.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:04.760
And whatever killed this one...

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:07.920
Oh, who knows.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:14.640
We've got to wait and find out what killed it before we jump to any conclusions.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.240
Frank wants to find out how she died.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:31.640
There's no visible wounds.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:32.480
No visible.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:36.240
So, it may well have been a snake.

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:41.600
A terrible tragedy right here.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.760
He calls the lion expert to confirm the identity of the lioness.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.320
All right.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.160
OK.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.400
Bye.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:56.360
So...yeah, it's Nabo.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.960
Yeah, I think it's Nabo.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:13:01.440
This is the first lioness that Saba identified.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:07.800
Nabo is the grandmother of the young cubs Saba saw this morning.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.080
Saba's going to be devastated to hear this.

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:27.920
Saba is arriving at the bush clinic with the sick man.

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:31.720
Jambo, jambo.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:34.600
She's concerned that Latoya has malaria.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:37.520
If he does, it has to be treated quickly.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:41.160
So, this has developed overnight because yesterday he was fine.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:47.160
The only way you can tell is looking for parasites in the blood.

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:57.040
No malaria.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.920
Why do you think he's having this stomach pain?

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:03.000
Gastric?

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.320
Yes.

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:06.880
It's a severe tummy bug.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:10.800
The doctor's prescribed a course of antibiotics and sent Latoya home to rest.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.200
OK, thank you.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:12.440
Bye.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:29.240
Back at the research centre, Frank is preparing to break the news of Nabo's death to Saba.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:35.680
Without Nabo to watch over them, the family is now much weaker.

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:44.800
Young cubs like these are vulnerable to attack by roving males, who will kill any cub that isn't their own.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:51.200
Nabo's death means there are fewer lionesses to keep the cubs safe.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:57.720
Hello.

00:14:56.760 --> 00:15:01.080
Hey, Sabs, how are you doing?

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.440
Hi, baby.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:03.680
I've got some bad news, I'm afraid.

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:08.240
This lion that was injured, it was your lioness.

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:12.120
It was the lioness you first... identified with Shiv.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:14.800
Nabo?

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:15.400
Nabo.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:17.400
She's dead?

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.920
She's dead.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.240
She's dead?!

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:19.680
She's dead.

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:20.720
I'm sorry, baby.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:34.400
Life on this frontier is dangerous, even for lions.

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:43.600
You don't get more fearless than a lioness... ..and yet she's just gone down, perhaps through a snakebite.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:46.720
Seems like one of the more likely explanations.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:53.560
With snakes around, Frank is worried about the girls.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:16:01.440
It does make you think about Selkie running around here and how easy it would be for her to get bitten.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:03.240
I'm glad we've got the Warriors to stick around the kids.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:11.360
They're like a mobile safety fence, in that they'll make sure that most of the dangers are out of the way.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:17.240
Samburu warrior Nporian knows all about snakes.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:28.680
He wants to teach the girls how to avoid dangers in the bush.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:42.200
There are scorpions to watch out for and ant lions hiding under your feet.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:47.000
Warriors grow up bush-wise.

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:51.520
Their survival depends on being able to read the signs of animal life around them.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:56.800
Everything they need can be found here.

00:16:56.920 --> 00:17:05.839
One tree provides a weapon... ..another provides a toothbrush.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:20.400
With Nporian's help, the girls are learning how to avoid the dangers all around them... ..and how to look good in the bush!

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:31.720
It's been a long day.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:39.960
For the children it's time for bed, but Saba still has guests to take care of.

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:41.960
Well, my job is sort of partly to...

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:46.200
You know, I'm running the camp, so I am keeping all the logistics going.

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:50.760
Then, in the evening, when they come back after their game drives, it's my turn to be the hostess.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:59.760
So, you know, I make sure they're all OK, and we sit down and tell stories, and do my best to make them feel very passionate about Samburu.

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.760
OK...

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.480
Ready to face the music.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:07.960
Saba's problems are not over yet.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:13.560
The solar system is still down and the freezers aren't freezing.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:28.880
Chef Serena is treating the guests to a traditional Samburu dinner.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:19:06.760
The food may be tasty, but without electricity the guests are eating by firelight.

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:22.200
Saba hopes the romantic setting will distract them from the power shortage.

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:41.080
They've pulled it off, but Saba must make sure she gets the power back on soon.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:54.080
This morning, the guest's day is starting early.

00:19:53.240 --> 00:20:00.360
Hello.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:00.720
Hello.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.560
Good morning.

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:09.960
Wildlife guide Serenoy has an important mission ahead.

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:17.840
These guests are from America and Saba wants to make sure they see the Koitagor lion pride.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:22.880
..Those two tiny little cubs.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:27.040
I think they're a bit lion-crazy, so it would be really wonderful...

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:28.480
Good luck today.

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:36.040
Serenoy is heading to the area where Saba saw them.

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:46.120
It's very difficult to find lions right now, so, you know, I have a lot of pressure because... these clients are crazy about lions and I have to find them.

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:55.320
Samburu's lions live in smaller prides than elsewhere in Africa.

00:20:54.360 --> 00:21:01.800
Here the females and their cubs team up, while males move between several groups.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:11.360
Pride-mates can spend months or even years apart, so both sexes need to be much more self-reliant.

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:14.760
This could be why Samburu's males have such patchy manes.

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:24.720
A huge necklace of fur is a handicap in thorny scrub and a low profile ensures better hunting.

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:34.480
So, to see the lions, especially in this environment where there are so many who you have worked so hard to see a population of lions being restored, it would make it very special.

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:43.360
Guests come here for the wildlife, but they also expect luxury.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:54.600
Saba must make sure the camp lives up to expectations, but a power shortage at the start of high season is a big problem.

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:56.360
Good morning, guys.

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:57.560
Good morning.

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:01.640
Luckily, energy expert Bart Fugars has returned with new solar panels.

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:05.760
It's like a new horizon, a new dawn, on the power front.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:14.120
What we're doing today is we're boosting our whole system, so that the batteries are going to get this major power set.

00:22:14.280 --> 00:22:16.840
Slowly, slowly...

00:22:15.880 --> 00:22:20.160
Bernard is on hand to oversee the installation.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:21.720
This is not an easy job.

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:26.720
It's extremely delicate because it could collapse, then...we're done.

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:30.760
Then we have to depend on the moonlight...

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:31.280
..and the stars.

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:33.720
I'll leave you guys to it.

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:34.200
See you later.

00:22:45.640 --> 00:22:52.320
Out in the reserve, wildlife guide Serenoy is searching for the lions.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:56.960
He's watching the prey animals to see if they've spotted anything.

00:22:57.480 --> 00:23:00.280
FEMALE They are definitely seeing something.

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:01.840
Giraffes will tell you...

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:06.960
It's only two things - either they have seen lion or when they see human beings - those are things that makes giraffe be watchful.

00:23:06.200 --> 00:23:09.000
Look at them all standing at attention.

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:09.800
Yes.

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:12.800
WOMAN Maybe it's lions!

00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:12.920
Yeah, it may be lions.

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:13.880
Can we go there and see if there are lions there?

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:14.600
Yes.

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:14.920
Yes.

00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:15.200
Look, look!

00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:16.600
Simba.

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:24.200
My gosh, look.

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:33.800
I've never seen this kind of behaviour before, where the lions would stay under the bush and the giraffes would gather and watch them like that.

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:37.600
They are really interested in the lions.

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:42.320
They are.

00:23:41.360 --> 00:23:44.480
Samburu is quite special.

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:54.120
Serenoy has found several members of Nabo's pride and the lone pride male, who is normally extremely elusive.

00:23:53.960 --> 00:24:00.880
Two miles away, Saba is searching for the rest of the pride.

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:10.760
She's desperate to find out how the young lionesses are managing without Nabo.

00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:12.000
There's a lion, darling.

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:12.640
Look!

00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:13.560
Look-look.

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:15.320
Do you see the female there?

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:15.800
Yeah.

00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:16.240
That's a lioness.

00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:18.960
Isn't that exciting?

00:24:18.040 --> 00:24:19.160
Yeah.

00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:24.520
This is where they really, really, really like to come.

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:27.280
..See cubs!

00:24:27.680 --> 00:24:30.680
You want to see the cubs?

00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:31.200
Yeah.

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:33.040
Well, if we wait here, maybe they'll come.

00:24:33.840 --> 00:24:36.160
And you know who she is?

00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:36.480
Nm-nm.

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:36.600
She's part of their family.

00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:36.960
Oh.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.440
She's their auntie.

00:24:42.320 --> 00:24:43.960
Look, look, look!

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:45.720
She's seen something.

00:24:44.840 --> 00:24:46.280
Maybe she...

00:24:45.520 --> 00:24:48.360
Look, there's some impala.

00:24:47.680 --> 00:24:49.080
You see them coming down to the river?

00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:49.600
Oh, yeah.

00:24:48.840 --> 00:24:50.360
There, in-between.

00:24:52.040 --> 00:24:57.640
She's seen them and she's thinking that's exactly where she wants them to go, so she can try and catch them.

00:24:56.960 --> 00:24:59.280
She's coming, she's coming...

00:24:58.320 --> 00:25:00.080
Look, she's trotting towards us.

00:24:59.320 --> 00:25:03.440
Now, you see how she's coming up near the edge of the river bank?

00:25:04.200 --> 00:25:05.520
Look how she's stalking.

00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:10.560
She's going super-slowly because she doesn't want anything to see her.

00:25:16.560 --> 00:25:18.920
I'm going to get up ahead a little bit, so we can be in the right position.

00:25:23.120 --> 00:25:27.240
See the guinea fowl as well?

00:25:26.400 --> 00:25:27.560
They're all alarming.

00:25:26.720 --> 00:25:29.480
They're telling the other animals that the lion is here.

00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:30.040
They're all making their alarm call.

00:25:35.280 --> 00:25:37.200
She's got it!

00:25:44.480 --> 00:25:51.640
Saba wants to teach the girls about the realities of life and death in the bush.

00:25:50.880 --> 00:25:57.600
She's going to be so tired after this because, you know, she's doing this all on her own.

00:25:57.160 --> 00:25:59.520
Isn't that amazing?

00:25:58.640 --> 00:26:00.280
Yeah.

00:25:59.400 --> 00:26:08.120
For this to happen right in front of us now, with the three kids in the car when we're least expecting it, is seriously amazing!

00:26:07.160 --> 00:26:08.480
It's great news for Nabo's family.

00:26:11.120 --> 00:26:20.720
This lioness has proved to be a phenomenal hunter, able to bring down large prey on her own.

00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:29.200
She's been well-taught by her mother and will pass on the same skills to the cubs.

00:26:28.280 --> 00:26:35.880
Nabo's grandchildren will be fine.

00:26:37.040 --> 00:26:46.080
Back at camp, the team is putting the finishing touches to the solar panels.

00:26:45.200 --> 00:26:47.280
Saba?

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:49.960
Saba has returned just in time to see Bernard's handiwork.

00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:54.560
Are you finished?

00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:55.920
We've finished, yes.

00:26:54.960 --> 00:26:56.920
Let's go and have a look, then.

00:26:55.960 --> 00:26:57.000
OK.

00:26:57.440 --> 00:26:58.600
It's done.

00:26:59.240 --> 00:27:00.760
Oh, great!

00:26:59.840 --> 00:27:01.760
Yeah.

00:27:01.080 --> 00:27:03.920
Oh, my goodness, look at all those lovely green lights.

00:27:03.120 --> 00:27:04.560
Yeah.

00:27:03.600 --> 00:27:04.720
That is fantastic.

00:27:03.760 --> 00:27:05.440
So, hopefully, that's our problems over.

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:05.760
One problem solved in the bush.

00:27:08.400 --> 00:27:09.720
Brilliant.

00:27:08.920 --> 00:27:11.040
Well done.

00:27:10.280 --> 00:27:12.800
Thank you so much.

00:27:13.080 --> 00:27:20.640
With the freezers back up and running, normal dinner service is resumed.

00:27:22.640 --> 00:27:27.160
Fingers crossed, but everything looks like it's working.

00:27:26.200 --> 00:27:32.480
And, for the first time in a very long time, I have three functioning cooling units.

00:27:31.600 --> 00:27:36.120
It says, "Please leave me alone."

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:36.440
Do not disturb!

00:27:35.920 --> 00:27:37.840
Quite right.

00:27:36.880 --> 00:27:38.080
Ever!

00:27:37.200 --> 00:27:39.560
Never, never, never.

00:27:39.840 --> 00:27:43.720
We're paranoid about losing the...the coldness now.

00:27:43.600 --> 00:27:46.320
It's been such a battle.

00:27:45.640 --> 00:27:46.840
I know.

00:27:45.880 --> 00:27:47.080
But now it's...

00:27:46.200 --> 00:27:47.640
It seems it's working.

00:27:46.680 --> 00:27:51.640
We've now got two fridges - one for food and one for drinks, so it...couldn't be better.

00:27:51.160 --> 00:27:52.440
And I just hope it lasts.

00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:53.280
All is good.

00:27:58.880 --> 00:28:00.680
Hello, everybody.

00:27:59.720 --> 00:28:01.840
Are you all OK?

00:28:02.280 --> 00:28:12.640
With power restored, camp is ready to cope with the demands of the season ahead... ..and Saba can get back to her guests.

00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:18.280
Next time, high season is in full swing...

00:28:17.440 --> 00:28:19.000
Everything has to be...super!

00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:21.320
Super, super, super.

00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:23.160
..But drought forces the main attraction to leave the reserve.

00:28:22.440 --> 00:28:29.120
It becomes a bit of a challenge for us because, you know, there aren't that many elephants.

00:28:28.200 --> 00:28:31.200
The elephants are heading into danger.

00:28:30.400 --> 00:28:36.760
Poachers were spotted this morning and they ran from their camp.

00:28:35.920 --> 00:28:41.560
Frank's battle to protect them becomes dangerous.

00:28:41.040 --> 00:28:43.240
They're out there.

00:28:44.920 --> 00:28:46.280
They're right on the front line.
